sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Auth as Kuadrant/Authorino<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant API as API Server<br/>8000/TCP HTTP(S)
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP
    participant Redis as Redis/Valkey<br/>6379/TCP
    participant S3 as S3 Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Proc as Processor<br/>(Worker Pool)
    participant Router as llm-d Router<br/>HTTP(S)
    participant GC as Garbage Collector

    Note over Client,GC: Flow 1: Batch Job Submission

    Client->>Auth: POST /v1/files (multipart/form-data)<br/>Auth: API key / SA token
    Auth->>API: Forward + inject X-MaaS-Username header
    API->>S3: Upload input file<br/>TLS 1.2+ / AWS IAM
    S3-->>API: File stored (tenant-scoped path)
    API->>PG: INSERT file metadata<br/>TLS (configurable)
    PG-->>API: File ID
    API-->>Auth: 200 OK (file object)
    Auth-->>Client: File upload response

    Client->>Auth: POST /v1/batches<br/>Auth: API key / SA token
    Auth->>API: Forward + inject tenant header
    API->>PG: INSERT batch record<br/>TLS (configurable)
    PG-->>API: Batch ID
    API->>Redis: ZADD to priority queue<br/>TLS (optional)
    Redis-->>API: Queued
    API-->>Auth: 200 OK (batch object)
    Auth-->>Client: Batch created response

    Note over Client,GC: Flow 2: Batch Job Execution

    Proc->>Redis: BZPOPMIN from priority queue<br/>TLS (optional)
    Redis-->>Proc: Job dequeued
    Proc->>PG: UPDATE batch status → in_progress<br/>TLS (configurable)
    Proc->>S3: Download input file<br/>TLS 1.2+ / AWS IAM
    S3-->>Proc: JSONL input data

    loop For each inference request (up to 50,000)
        Proc->>Router: POST inference request<br/>Auth: Bearer API key<br/>AIMD concurrency control
        Router-->>Proc: Inference result
    end

    Proc->>S3: Upload output file<br/>TLS 1.2+ / AWS IAM
    S3-->>Proc: Output stored
    Proc->>PG: UPDATE batch status → completed<br/>TLS (configurable)
    Proc->>Redis: Publish completion event

    Note over Client,GC: Flow 3: Status Query

    Client->>Auth: GET /v1/batches/{batch_id}<br/>Auth: API key / SA token
    Auth->>API: Forward + inject tenant header
    API->>PG: SELECT batch record (WHERE tenant_id = ?)
    API->>Redis: GET real-time progress counters
    Redis-->>API: In-flight counts
    PG-->>API: Batch metadata
    API-->>Auth: 200 OK (batch with progress)
    Auth-->>Client: Batch status response

    Note over Client,GC: Flow 4: Garbage Collection

    GC->>PG: SELECT expired batches/files<br/>TLS (configurable)
    PG-->>GC: Expired records
    GC->>S3: DELETE expired file content<br/>TLS 1.2+ / AWS IAM
    S3-->>GC: Deleted
    GC->>PG: DELETE expired metadata
    GC->>Redis: Cleanup stale queue/in-flight entries
